AMENDMENT TO REGIONAL REGULATION OF BANTUL REGENCY

REGENT OF BANTUL

SPECIAL REGION OF YOGYAKARTA

NUMBER 15 OF 2015

CONCERNING

AMENDMENT TO REGIONAL REGULATION OF BANTUL REGENCY NUMBER 15 OF 2013 CONCERNING PROTECTION OF CHILDREN AND WOMEN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF BANTUL,

Considering:

a. that based on clarification from the Governor of the Special Region of Yogyakarta, several provisions in Regional Regulation of Bantul Regency Number 15 of 2013 concerning Protection of Children and Women Victims of Violence need to be improved by amending the Regional Regulation;
b. that based on the consideration as referred to in letter a, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Amendment to Regional Regulation of Bantul Regency Number 15 of 2013 concerning Protection of Children and Women Victims of Violence;

In View of:

1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 15 of 1950 concerning Formation of Regency Regions Within the Special Region of Jogjakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 44);
3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);
4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606).
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
6. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
7. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4976);
8. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);
9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
10. Government Regulation Number 32 of 1950 concerning Stipulation of the Effective Date of Laws of 1950 Numbers 12, 13, 14 and 15 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 59);
11. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);
12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning Implementation of Women Protection;
13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 Concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Child Protection;
14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Handling Child Victims of Violence;
17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence;
18. Regional Regulation of the Special Region of Yogyakarta Province Number 3 of 2012 concerning Protection of Children and Women Victims of Violence (Regional Gazette of the Special Region of Yogyakarta Province of 2012 Number 3, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of the Special Region of Yogyakarta Province Number 3);
19. Regional Regulation of Bantul Regency Number 15 of 2013 concerning Protection of Children and Women Victims of Violence (Regional Gazette of Bantul Regency of 2013 Number 15, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Bantul Regency Number 28);

With Mutual Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BANTUL REGENCY,

and

REGENT OF BANTUL,

HAS DECIDED:

To Establish:
REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING AMENDMENT TO REGIONAL REGULATION OF BANTUL REGENCY NUMBER 15 OF 2013 CONCERNING PROTECTION OF CHILDREN AND WOMEN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE.

Article 2

The principles of organizing protection for children and women from acts of violence are:
a. respect for and fulfillment of the rights of victims;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. the best interests of victims; and
e. empowerment.

3. The provisions of Article 3 are amended to read as follows:

Article 3

1. Forms of violence include, among others:
a. physical;
b. psychological;
c. sexual;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/or
f. other violence.
2. The objectives of protecting Children and Women from acts of violence are:
a. to prevent and eliminate all forms of acts of violence and exploitation against children and women occurring in the family and community environment;
b. to pursue recovery and social reintegration of children and women victims of violence;
c. to provide services to children and women victims of acts of violence, reporters, and witnesses;
d. to empower women victims of violence; and
e. to increase community participation.
3. The organization of protection for children and women from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) includes the following aspects:
a. prevention;
b. services and assistance;
c. social reintegration; and
d. empowerment.

4. The provisions of Article 6 are amended to read as follows:

Article 6

The organization of protection for children and women victims of violence is the obligation of:
a. the Regional Government;
b. the Village Government;
c. the community;
d. the family; and
e. parents.

5. The provisions of letters d and e of paragraph (1) of Article 7 are amended to read as follows:

Article 7

1. To implement the provisions as referred to in Article 6 letter a, the Regional Government carries out victim protection efforts in the form of:
a. formulating policies on the protection of Children and Women from all forms of acts of violence and discrimination;
b. preparing program and activity planning;
c. providing infrastructure and facilities support;
d. allocating a special gender-responsive budget that supports the protection of children and women victims of violence;
e. establishing and facilitating PPT;
f. establishing and facilitating FPKK; and
g. conducting monitoring and evaluation.
2. In implementing the obligations of the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government prepares a Regional Action Plan as a basis for SKPD in implementing protection for victims.
3. The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2) is part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD).
4. Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2) are further regulated by Regent Regulation.
6. The title of Part One of CHAPTER IV is deleted.

7. The provisions of Article 13 are amended to read as follows:

Article 40

1. In an effort to provide and organize handling of services and protection for victims, the Regional Government and Village Government establish FPKK.
2. FPKK as referred to in paragraph (1) aims to:
a. carry out efforts to prevent the occurrence of cases of violence;
b. coordinate and synchronize the handling of PPT services;
c. maintain and develop networks and referral systems; and
d. collect, compile and present reports on cases of violence.
3. The management and membership of the Regency FPKK are established by Regent Decree and the Village FPKK is established by Village Head Decree.
4. The membership of FPKK as referred to in paragraph (3) is grouped into the following roles:
a. health role;
b. psychology role;
c. legal role;
d. social role; and
e. economic role.
5. Further provisions regarding the establishment, duties, principal tasks, and functions as well as membership of FPKK as referred to in paragraph (1) are regulated by Regent Regulation.

11. The provisions of Article 44 are amended to become Article 43 to read as follows:
